-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Truncated HOSVD:** Standard truncated Higher-Order SVD (HOSVD) does not hold the optimal property of truncated SVD, but yields a quasi-optimal solution sufficient for practical use [S1].
-*   **Rank Selection:** The choice of rank involves a trade-off between model size and rendering quality. Too low a rank may lose important details, while too high a rank increases storage and computation [S1].
+**Parameters:**
+*   **Rank Truncation:** The number of components kept in the decomposition determines the model size and detail level. Lower ranks preserve primary information due to rank-residual learning [S1].
+*   **Ratio of Vector- to Matrix-based Components:** Controllable to trade off between model size and performance [S1].
+
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Truncated HOSVD:** Standard truncated HOSVD does not hold the optimal property of truncated SVD, but yields a quasi-optimal solution sufficient for practical use [S1].
